  If you're not playing a speed character, but just want to speed
through Gehennom, there are refinements to this technique.
Teleportitis, scrolls of teleport, and wands of digging can help 
save mana, so the Eye of Aethiopica isn't as important.

  If the stairs are relatively close, use wands of digging and
walk.  That saves mana.  Two or three wands of digging should be
all you need to take with you when you escape the dungeon.  Even
if you need to free yourself from frozen lava on the Plane of 
Fire.  Or if you want to make pits blocking doorways on the 
Astral Plane, or even break a wand of digging or two on Astral
to block large areas.  (Hey, break a wand of digging, then break 
out your polearm!)

Add teleportitis and you'll get free teleports while walking (and
save more mana.)  

  Bring every scroll of teleportation you've found so far as 
well.  Adjust them to 'r'.  Then instead of ^T you can 'rr' 
instead.  More mana saved.  (NB: Scrolls of teleport don't work 
on any of the Planes.)

  I use scrolls of teleport, instead of ^T, throughout the
Dungeons of Doom in addition to Gehennom.  I still usually leave 
a stack of ten or so scrolls of teleport by the upstairs on Dlvl 
1 when I leave with the AoY.  (NB: Don't try to use scrolls of
teleport on no teleport levels.)


